list.item:
 Jiang Jieshi (Chiang Kai-shek), President of the
ROC until April 5, 1975; Chairman, ROC National Security Council until 1975;
Director-General, Kuomintang, until 1975

person.note:
Ambassador to Korea until August 19, 1974; Assistant Secretary of State for
                    East Asian and Pacific Affairs from September 27, 1974 until June 30, 1976;
                    Under Secretary of State for Political Affairs from July 1, 1976

member of the NSC Operations Staff/East Asia
                    until April 1973; Co-Deputy Chief of Mission in Beijing from 1973 to 1975;
                    Ambassador to Singapore from August 1975

PRC Ambassador to France until March 1973;
                    Chief of the PRC Liaison Office in the United
                    States from March 1973

President of the ROC until April 5, 1975;
                    Chairman, ROC National Security Council until
                    1975; Director-General, Kuomintang, until 1975

Prince and cousin of Norodom Sihanouk;
                    ally of Lon Nol; Deputy Prime Minister,
                    then member of the High Political Council, from 1970 to 1974

Premier of the PRC until January 8, 1976;
                    member, Standing Committee of the Chinese Communist Party’s Political Bureau
                    until 1976
